<title>SINGAPORE: Insurance Corp H1 net falls.</title>
<headline>Insurance Corp H1 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30 1996</p>
<p>		    (in million S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     6.65  vs	  7.35</p>
<p>    Dividend  (cents)		    3.00  vs	  3.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		   13.21  vs	 14.63</p>
<p>    Group shr fully diluted (cents) 12.87  vs	 14.33</p>
<p>    Turnover			     132.79  vs	126.93</p>
<p>    Group Investment income	    3.40  vs	  4.06</p>
<p>    Group other income (including    2.37  vs	  1.61</p>
<p>    interest)</p>
<p>    Profit on sale of investments   4.61   vs	  2.23</p>
<p>    Profit before tax		  10.12   vs	 10.77</p>
<p> Depreciation, amor (loss)	    1.10   vs	  1.04</p>
<p>    Tax				    2.35    vs	  2.33</p>
<p>Minorities (loss)			0.02    vs	  0.04</p>
<p>    Last Day Books Open	    Sept 16 1996</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date		October 2 1996</p>
<p>Note- Full name of the company is the Insurance Corporation of Singapore Ltd</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
